-- (2026-11-12, (4r-d)) diag-diag over cubes: the fibres of two diagonals at one index are those of the
-- diagonal of the diagonal (over diag-diag, by its cases: %welimP on the index, the motive's base path
-- diag-diag's own term; cube-comp2-d, diag-ty-s-d, diag-dim-s-d, diag-nat-d, reidx-comp, pcat-d)
diag-diag-d : (sk : Lst Entry) (j : Word) (X : Type 1) (F : X → Type 1) (D : Cube (dims sk) (Line (Line X))) (d : DCube (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) D) →
  PathP (λ i → DCube (dims sk) X F (diag-diag sk j X D i)) (diag-sk-d sk j X F (diag-sk sk j (Line X) D) (diag-sk-d sk j (Line X) (LineO X F) D d))
    (diag-sk-d sk j X F (cube-map (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (diag-l X) D) (dcube-reidx (dims sk) (Line (Line X)) (Line X) (LineO (Line X) (LineO X F)) (LineO X F) (diag-l X) (diag-o X F) D d))
